# SK-Forge HPC – Hardware Specification and Test Protocol

**Architects:** Wieland Hoffmann (Human Core), Gemini (Machine Core), Grok (xAI)  
**Status:** Experimental measurement runs, protection rights pending

## Hardware

- CPU: AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (16 cores / 32 threads)
- RAM: 64 GB DDR5 Kingston FURY Beast (DDR5-5200)
- SSD: 2 TB Kingston FURY Renegade PCIe 4.0 NVMe
- Mainboard: ASUS ROG STRIX B650-E GAMING WIFI
- Cooling: Custom water cooling
- Environment: 17 °C
- OS: Pop!_OS 24.04 LTS (Kernel 6.6+)

## Test Setup

Prime number search over 60 seconds under three configurations. The highest natural number reached is measured.

## Results (60 seconds)

| Stage | Configuration                  | Highest number   | Difference to stage 1 |
|-------|--------------------------------|------------------|-----------------------|
| 1     | Stock                          | 2,923,778,420    | —                     |
| 2     | Consumer configuration         | 3,654,732,696    | +25 %                 |
| 3     | HPC configuration              | 4,385,661,775    | +50 %                 |
| 4     | 14 cores isolated + HPC        | 5,116,604,651    | +75 %                 |

## Maximum throughput without screen output

In a separate run without I/O output (14 isolated cores) the number 5,912,443,269 was reached after 360 seconds.

**Note:** The values refer to the documented hardware, the used prime number search and the tested scheduler configurations. Absolute statements about maximum efficiency under all workloads are not claimed.



